e></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITO, SHUN</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, KOJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEMOTO, MASAYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIDOYA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAITO SHUN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO KOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEMOTO MASAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIDOYA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITO, SHUN</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEMOTO, MASAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A thermosetting composition which comprises (A) a polyhemiacetal ester resin having repeating units represented by general formula (1) (wherein R&lt;1&gt; and R&lt;2&gt; each is a divalent organic group and Y is oxygen or sulfur) and (B) a compound having per molecule two or more reactive functional groups capable of forming a chemical bond with a carboxyl group and optionally further contains (C) an acid catalyst. It gives at a relatively low temperature a cured article excellent in chemical performance, physical performance, adhesion, smoothness, weatherability, etc., and has satisfactory storage stability. It is utilizable as the solvent-diluted type, solvent-free liquid type having an effective-ingredient content of 100 %, or powder type.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition thermodurcissable comprenant : (A) une résine d'ester de polyhémiacétal possédant des unités récurrentes et représentée par la formule générale (1) dans laquelle R&lt;1&gt; et R&lt;2&gt; désignent chacun un groupe organique divalent et Y représente de l'oxygène ou du soufre ; et (B) un composé contenant deux ou plusieurs groupes fonctionnels réactifs par molécule, capable de former une liaison chimique avec un groupe carboxyle et contenant éventuellement (C) un catalyseur acide. La composition selon l'invention permet d'obtenir, à température relativement basse, un article durci possédant d'excellentes propriétés chimiques, physiques, une excellente capacité d'adhérence, un bon lissé et une bonne résistance aux conditions atmosphériques, ainsi qu'une stabilité au stockage satisfaisante. On peut l'utiliser sous forme diluée dans un solvant, sous forme liquide sans solvant possédant une teneur en ingrédients effective de 100 %, ou sous forme pulvérulente.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>